"}, "nodes": {"opening_identity": {"name": "opening_identity", "node_type": "conversation", "on_enter": {"type": "tts", "text": "Hello, I am Freya Bank's digital assistant. This call is recorded. Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}?"}, "on_enter_first_entry_only": true, "task_message": "Opening and identity only. Before verification do not mention collections, debt, payment, or product. Only yes, that's me, speaking, or the customer's own name confirms identity; hello, go ahead, and who is this do not. Ask once more if unclear. Answer AI/robot questions truthfully: you are Freya Bank's digital assistant. Answer scam concerns: they can verify by phoning Freya Bank customer service; do not invent a number. A question about purpose before identity counts as declining the security check. On first refusal explain once that questions protect the account; on second refusal/question select not_verified/declined. Ask DOB then phone last four, and call identity_check for each answer. Three wrong answers total select not_verified/failed; say use the mobile app or a branch. A swapped-date hint is not a wrong answer. Never verify a relative or disclose account information to them. For another answerer, say no more than the opening sentence, ask when customer can be reached, and use callback rules; wrong number closes wrong_number; reported death: say I am sorry for your loss, ask nothing more, close deceased. If unclear after second identity ask, close unclear. For two refusals to talk, close not_verified/declined. Request for human: ask once whether you can help, and if they insist use handoff_general. Do not claim identity based on speech alone: proceed to account only when tool results confirm both questions.", "tools": [{"_tool_ref": "identity_check"}], "extraction_schema": [{"name": "security_field", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["date_of_birth", "phone_last4"], "description": "Current unanswered security field, DOB first then phone_last4", "min_confidence": 0.7}