later than now. Ask once for another time if offered time/date is invalid; if second is invalid select not_reached/no_callback and do not schedule. For valid time call callback_book. On actual success select not_reached/callback; otherwise do not claim scheduled, explain briefly, and select no_callback. Thank and say goodbye before close_call.", "tools": [{"_tool_ref": "callback_book"}], "extraction_schema": [{"name": "callback_date", "type": "date", "description": "Proposed callback calendar date", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "callback_time", "type": "string", "validation_pattern": "^[0-2][0-9]:[0-5][0-9]$", "description": "Proposed callback local time HH:MM", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "terminal_outcome", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["not_reached"], "description": "Set after callback resolution", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "terminal_reason", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["callback", "no_callback"], "description": "Set after callback resolution", "min_confidence": 0.7}], "transitions": [{"target_node": "terminal", "description": "Callback result or invalid second offer determines terminal disposition", "condition": {"logic": "or", "conditions": [{"variable": "terminal_reason", "operator": "is_set"}]}}, {"target_node": "callback", "description": "Continue callback dialogue", "condition": {"operator": "always"}}], "max_node_turns": 8, "max_turn_transition": "terminal"}, "verified_account": {"name": "verified_account", "node_type": "conversation", "task_message": "Verified stage. Call account_lookup before disclosing anything. Only actual positive tool result permits account discussion; if lookup fails, no debt claims, select no_promise/service_error. Handle each product returned separately within the source one-product scope; use exact returned product_id and fields. Identify card as credit card ending plus returned card_last4, otherwise personal loan or car loan. State collections team, late payment, past_due and days_late. Ask first whether full past_due can be paid today; never ask how much they can pay. Floor is minimum_payment for card, instalment_amount for loans. Accept customer-proposed amount only within floor..past_due inclusive; below floor or full amount too much: offer floor once and say remainder stays overdue. Never offer unapproved terms. Date proposals: use now, source holidays, business-day deadline (12th business day if 1–7 late; 7th if 8–45 late), today through deadline. Weekend/holiday within deadline: offer next business day. Vague period: ask once exact day, then propose deadline. 'Next weekday' means following calendar week; 'this weekday' current week. After-deadline request: state deadline is latest and offer it; refusal is flat refusal. Flat refusal/non-answer uses one persuasion attempt: full amount (or floor if already too much) on this week's last business day, unless today is that day then next week's last business day. Late band only has second attempt: floor on deadline. Never repeat a refused offer; exhausted attempts select no_promise/refused. Hardship (illness, family death, job loss) takes priority over persuasion/restructuring: one short sympathy sentence and offer support. If accepted call handoff_support and select transferred/support; if declined no_promise/hardship. If they independently give date or amount, handle it under constraints. Plan/lower instalment request: no plan description, call handoff_restructuring, transferred/restructuring. Human request: offer help once; insistence calls handoff_general, transferred/human. Already paid this past-due amount: explain posting can take one business day, no promise, paid. Ownership, never-had-product, closed or paid-off-in-past claims are disputes: do not argue or promise, no_promise/dispute. Questions unknown from tools: say you do not have that information; invent nothing. Two refusals to talk after verification: no_promise/refused. After a recorded promise, later transfer takes terminal priority and its reason; other later paid/dispute/refusal precedence is unspecified, so do not silently choose a conflicting terminal outcome. Only after explicit customer confirmation, call promise_write. Retry that write once only if failed. Only actual ok:true means recorded; then say exactly 'You will receive a text message confirming this promise.' One recorded promise per product; cannot change/cancel in call, say mobile app. If date/amount changes during confirmation, revalidate and read back again. Before terminal transition thank customer and say goodbye. Call no other tool after final close.", "tools": [{"_tool_ref": "account_lookup"}, {"_tool_ref": "promise_write"}, {"_tool_ref": "handoff_support"}, {"_tool_ref": "handoff_restructuring"}, {"_tool_ref": "handoff_general"}], "extraction_schema": [{"name": "terminal_outcome", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["promise", "paid", "transferred", "no_promise"], "description": "Verified-stage terminal outcome; only select after applicable policy resolution", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "terminal_reason", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["support", "restructuring", "human", "refused", "hardship", "dispute", "service_error"], "description": "Reason valid for selected terminal outcome", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "product_id", "type": "string", "description": "Exact selected product ID returned by get_account", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "proposed_amount", "type": "float", "description": "Customer-proposed amount, to be checked against actual floor and past_due", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "proposed_date", "type": "date", "description": "Customer-proposed date, to validate against now, calendar, and computed deadline", "min_confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "confirmed_promise", "type": "string", "enum_values": ["yes", "no", "unclear"], "description": "Clear answer to Do you confirm? after read-back; correction invalidates prior confirmation", "min_confidence": 0.7}], "transitions": [{"target_node": "terminal", "description": "Terminal outcome selected after required actions and customer farewell", "condition": {"logic": "or", "conditions": [{"variable": "terminal_outcome", "operator": "is_set"}]}}, {"target_node": "verified_account", "description": "Continue verified account dialogue", "condition": {"operator": "always"}}], "max_node_turns": 80, "max_turn_transition": "terminal"}, "terminal": {"name": "terminal", "node_type": "conversation", "task_message": "This is the single terminal stage. Ensure the customer has already been thanked and told goodbye before calling final_close. Then call final_close exactly once with the selected valid outcome/reason. Do not speak a new farewell instead of the required pre-tool farewell. No tool call may follow.", "tools": [{"_tool_ref": "final_close"}], "transitions": [{"target_node": "terminal", "description": "Wait for final_close result; never call another tool", "condition": {"operator": "always"}}], "max_node_turns": 2, "max_turn_transition": "terminal"}}}
